# Coding Conventions

## Formatting & linting
- **Biome** is the only formatter and linter (`biome.json`). No ESLint, no Prettier.
- Line width 100, single quotes, semicolons, 2-space indent. `npx biome check --write` on changed files.
- Pre-commit checks run via **lefthook** (`lefthook.yml`) on **staged files only**; commit messages must be conventional (`<type>(<scope>): <subject>`).

## File & folder naming
- **kebab-case, always** for files and folders (e.g. `compensation-event-list-page.tsx`, `use-compensation-events.ts`).
- Export identifiers stay PascalCase — that is code, not file naming.

## New features: modular architecture
- New features live in `src/modules/<feature>/` as self-contained slices: `components/`, `hooks/`, `services/`, `types/`, `utils/`, `constants/`, plus an `index.ts` barrel.
- Consumers import from the module root only — no deep imports.
- Dependency direction is one-way: `components → hooks → services → AUSPIRA`. Components never call the API layer directly.
- Modules own their API endpoints in their own `constants/` — not in the shared `constants/api.constants.ts`.
- Reuse shared infrastructure (`AUSPIRA`, `buildUrl`, `IPaginatedApiResponse`) — don't re-implement.
- Reference implementation: `src/modules/compensation-event/`.

## UI rules
- **Raw Ant Design only.** Never the legacy X-wrappers (`ButtonX`, `InputX`, `CardX`, `TableX`, ...).
- **No Tailwind CSS, no custom CSS** inside modules, no inline styling beyond layout sizing (`style={{ width }}`).

## Comments
- Minimal. One-liner only when something is non-obvious. No JSDoc boilerplate.

## Testing
- Unit tests with Vitest, colocated under `src/tests/<feature>/` (`.test.ts`).
- Pure logic (utils/constants) must have tests.
